==== status
h2: High Availability Status
Real-time status of the HA cluster. Updates every 5 seconds.
h3: Cluster Status
| Cluster Overview
| Cluster State | STOPPED
| Node Role | UNKNOWN
| Last Synchronization
| Config Sync | Disabled
| Lease Sync | Disabled
h3: Service Status
| Service | Status | PID | Uptime
| keepalived | Running | <pid> | <uptime>
| owsync | Running | <pid> | <uptime>
| lease-sync | Running | <pid> | <uptime>
h3: Peer Status
<alert> No peers configured
==== simple
h2: High Availability - General
Configure a high availability cluster with 2 or more routers. Advanced options are available in the Advanced pages.
h3: Cluster Configuration
config.enabled [CBI.FlagValue] Enable HA Cluster: [ ]
  help: Enable high availability clustering on this router
config.node_priority [CBI.Value] Priority: value= (placeholder "100")
  help: VRRP priority (1-255). Higher priority becomes MASTER.
config.vrrp_transport [CBI.ListValue] VRRP Transport: select=multicast {multicast,unicast}
  help: Multicast is the default. Use unicast when multicast is unavailable on the network. Unicast adverts go to the peers below, from the first Source Address set: this fits only failover groups on the peers' network; another group sets its own unicast addresses in Advanced VRRP.
h3: Peer Routers
Other routers of the cluster. Configuration and lease sync run with every peer not marked VRRP only. In multicast mode, VRRP does not use this list.
| Peer | Role | 
| This section contains no values yet
<button> Add
h3: Virtual IP Addresses
All VIPs share a single failover group and switch together. Use the Advanced page to create independent failover groups. Multicast VRRP adds a second instance with VRID+128 for the IPv6 addresses. Unicast VRRP runs one instance in the family of the unicast addresses, and the other family fails over with it.
| Interface | VRID | IPv4 Address | IPv6 Address | Enable | 
| This section contains no values yet
<button> Add VIP...
h3: Synchronization
Keeps configuration files and DHCP leases identical on the cluster nodes. These settings must be the same on every node.
config.encryption_key [CBI.Value] Encryption Key: password= (placeholder "Click "Generate New Key" below to create a secure random key") button "∗"
  help: 256-bit AES key (64 hexadecimal characters), used for both configuration and lease sync. Must be identical on all nodes. Leave empty to sync in plaintext.
config._generate_key [CBI.ButtonValue] Generate New Key: button "Generate New Key"
h3: Configuration Files
config._group_dhcp [CBI.FlagValue] DHCP and DNS: [ ]
  help: /etc/config/dhcp: address pools, static leases, DNS settings.
config._group_firewall [CBI.FlagValue] Firewall: [ ]
  help: /etc/config/firewall: zones, rules, port forwards. Review the rules before enabling: they apply to every node.
h3: DHCP Leases
config.lease_sync [CBI.FlagValue] Real-time Lease Sync: [ ]
  help: Replicates DHCP leases between nodes so that clients keep their address after a failover. Independent of the DHCP configuration sync above.
==== keepalived-advanced
h2: High Availability - Advanced VRRP
Advanced VRRP instance tuning. VIPs and instance assignment are in General.
